      "math_academy_id": "q-22979",
      "knowledge_point_id": "bba0ad98-6940-502a-873c-8a589a03a499",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding Coterminal Angles in Degrees",
      "problem": "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =-{95}^{∘}?$\n\n- ${625}^{∘}$\n- ${160}^{∘}$\n- $-{455}^{∘}$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}:$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ to $-{95}^{∘}$:\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={265}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={625}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than ${625}^{∘}.$ So we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ from $-{95}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{455}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given angles, only ${625}^{∘}$ and $-{455}^{∘}$ are coterminal with $-{95}^{∘}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
